  "id": "EDU030",
  "title": "The Recommendation Echo Room",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "computing/data",
  "premise": "A curator wants a varied animation playlist, but a toy recommender only learns from the clips it already chose to show. An exploration lane exposes unseen options and reveals the feedback loop.",
  "hook": "What can this system learn from a choice it never offered?",
  "visible_action": "A recommendation carousel feeds clicks back into itself until an exploratory card enters from a separate lane.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Observed preferences can reflect what a system chose to expose.",
  "gate": "Label the algorithm invented; do not imply all recommendation systems behave identically.",
